    <string name="display_check">Display alignment check (visor)</string>
    <string name="visor_check_text">The patient looks at the phone screen directly, so this check is about orientation only. Start the preview and look at a door frame. Check three things: (1) the picture is upright; (2) raise your RIGHT hand, it must appear on the RIGHT and printed text must read normally; (3) roll your head, the white plumb line must stay on the real vertical edge. Fix each with the buttons below: Flip 180° for upside down, Mirror for left-right swapped, Rotation −1 if the picture turns the wrong way.</string>
    <string name="lens_check_text">1. Set the IPD to the wearer\'s measurement. 2. Start the preview, put the phone in the headset and look at a door frame or plumb line while rolling your head. The white plumb line must stay on the real vertical edge. If the camera image rotates the wrong way as you roll, flip the rotation direction.</string>
    <string name="start_preview">Start preview (Mode B at k = 1, plumb line)</string>
